Port (Rayman Origins PC, Android): no centroid interpolation of ps_1_x/ps_2_x colour inputs (D3D9's rule, which only
matters with MSAA). Measured on the Galaxy Tab S6 Lite (Adreno 618, Qualcomm driver) with tools/android/vkbench:
14 blended textured layers at 1280x720, 9.43 ms a frame with a centroid colour input, 3.52 ms without (2.7x a pixel).
The game's sprite shaders are ps_2_0 (texld * v0). DXVK_CENTROID=1 brings the centroid back. Apply after the others.

diff --git a/src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp b/src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp
index f7bd312..4334cc9 100644
--- a/src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp
+++ b/src/dxso/dxso_compiler.cpp
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include "../dxvk/dxvk_spec_const.h"
 
 #include <cfloat>
+#include <cstdlib>
 
 namespace dxvk {
 
@@ -636,7 +637,12 @@ namespace dxvk {
     const bool pixel  = m_programInfo.type() == DxsoProgramTypes::PixelShader;
     const bool vertex = !pixel;
 
-    if (pixel && input && semantic.usage == DxsoUsage::Color && m_programInfo.majorVersion() < 3)
+    // Port (Rayman Origins PC, Android): D3D9 interpolates ps_1_x/ps_2_x colour inputs at the centroid, which only
+    // differs from the pixel centre with MSAA. On the Galaxy Tab S6 Lite (Adreno 618, Qualcomm driver) a centroid
+    // input made each blended, textured pixel 2.7x slower without MSAA (tools/android/vkbench: 14 layers at 1280x720,
+    // 9.43 ms centroid, 3.52 ms not); the game's sprites are ps_2_0 (texld * v0). DXVK_CENTROID=1 brings it back.
+    static const bool s_centroid = [] { const char* e = std::getenv("DXVK_CENTROID"); return e && *e == '1'; }();
+    if (s_centroid && pixel && input && semantic.usage == DxsoUsage::Color && m_programInfo.majorVersion() < 3)
       centroid = true;
 
     uint32_t slot = 0;
